<title>USA: Champion Enterprises wins $11 mln bus pact.</title>
<headline>Champion Enterprises wins $11 mln bus pact.</headline>
<dateline>IMLAY CITY, Mich. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Champion Enterprises Inc said its motor coach subsidiary has received a contract valued at over $11 million to build 190 buses for New Jersey Transit.</p>
<p>The buses, will be built at the Champion Motor Coach plant in Imlay City, over a two-year period and will replace the existing jitney shuttle bus fleet being used in Atlantic City, N.J.</p>
<p>The buses will be Champion's Commodore model, which is built on General Motors Corp's Chevrolet P-30 commercial chassis.</p>
</text>
